We can express the decision rule as a threshold: $\text{start the venture}
=
\begin{cases}
1, & \text{necessity, preparation, and acceptable loss are all present},\\
0, & \text{otherwise}.
\end{cases}$ This is not a universal rule for all founders. It is a careful translation of Mitt’s local answer. The pressure to provide forced the question, but preparation made action possible.

