A cautious reconstruction is $E_{\text{remaining}}
=
E_{\text{day}}
-\sum_{i=1}^{n} c_i
-L_{\text{emotion}},$ where $c_i$ is the energy cost of the $i$-th communication, interaction, decision, or appointment, and $L_{\text{emotion}}$ is the additional loss from anger, frustration, or carryover. Mitt’s example is an appointment that goes badly: if we spend energy being upset, that waste affects the next appointment.

